#pragma once
// SetReplace's WolframModel (SetReplace 0.3.196) in single history under "EventOrderingFunction",
// recorded by reference/verify_setreplace_order.wls --record and read by
// hypergraph/tests/test_event_ordering.cpp. Events and expressions are numbered from 1 in
// creation order, as SetReplace's "AllEventsList" and "AllEventsEdgesList" are.
//
// kStream holds the cases in order. A case is: the event limit, the rule count, each rule's
// left-hand side and right-hand side, the initial state, the event count, each event (its rule
// from 1, the input count, the inputs, the output count, the outputs), the expressions, the
// causal pair count and the pairs (the event making an expression, then an event consuming
// it). An edge list is its edge count, then each edge as its arity and its vertices.

